## Git Workflow

### Branch Naming
Use descriptive names with type prefix:
- `feature/add-user-authentication` – New features
- `bugfix/fix-login-crash` – Bug fixes
- `docs/update-readme` – Documentation
- `refactor/simplify-api` – Refactoring

### Commit Format
```
[TYPE] Short description

Optional longer description if needed.

Examples:
[FEATURE] Add JWT authentication to API
[BUGFIX] Fix race condition in database query
[DOCS] Update API documentation
```

### Before Committing
- [ ] Run `npm test` – All tests pass
- [ ] Run `npm run lint` – No linting errors
- [ ] Update CHANGELOG.md if applicable
- [ ] Update documentation if behavior changed

### PR/Merge Checklist
- [ ] Tests pass locally
- [ ] Code is reviewed by at least one person
- [ ] Documentation updated
- [ ] No secrets or sensitive data in code
- [ ] Commit messages follow [TYPE] format

